  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n-  Widespread showers and seasonably cool temperatures persist\n   through the rest of the week and into early next week.\n\n-  Scattered thunderstorms on Saturday. \n\n-  60-80% chance that Sunday into Monday rainfall could exceed one\n   inch of additional rainfall from Missoula to northwest Montana!\n   50% chance that the Glacier Region experiences greater than\n   1.50\" of rain!\n \nVery impressive rainfall amounts have been observed across \nnorth- central Idaho in the last 24 hours...generally around one \ninch of rain fell from northwest of McCall to Grangeville to \nPierce! The heavier north to south oriented rainfall occurred as a\nspoke of energy will eventually move northwards into Canada later\nthis morning. As this occurs, the steady rain will give way to \npartly cloudy skies with scattered showers/isolated thunderstorms \nthis afternoon. \n\nRinse and repeat tonight? A fairly strong 100 knot jet aloft will\nprovide the lifting mechanism, interacting with a stalled frontal\nboundary to produce a mostly narrow southwest to northeast swath \nof steady moderate rain. Models shows this occurring from northern\nLemhi County north and east to northern Powell County. So if you\nare traveling east of Missoula, be prepared for wet and cold\nconditions as lows will generally be in the 40s. \n\nOn Saturday, with slightly warmer temperatures and possible breaks\nin the clouds, thunderstorms will be possible. Cloud cover will be\na limiting factor in their strength. Heavy rain, lightning, gusty\nwinds and small hail would be the main threats. \n\nThe upper low will continue to bring rain chances on Sunday into\nMonday across the region as it begins to depart to the east and\nnorth towards Saskatchewan, Canada by early Tuesday. The range of\nrainfall amounts purely from this period could range from 0.25\" \nto 1.00\" over Idaho and southwest Montana, and 0.50\" to 2.00\" \nacross northwest Montana!\n\nIt finally looks like we may have a few days to dry out a bit \nnext Tuesday through Thursday! The caveat could be that there \ncould be lingering clouds from all the moisture.",
